From c880a1392ac58e83de1b4add95f1c6ccc1e3b24c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:10:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(pocket): 2D Pocket runs on the path kernel behind
 the planner switch

The first recipe of K6 (#4023). Under CAMCRAFT_PLANNER=new the 2D Pocket
runs on the path kernel: Waterline (rings of the boundary, no load
control, each cut above the load named) and Offset rings (constant
engagement on the rings). Each Z level is planned by the stages with its
own heights, and the converter makes the plans into one toolpath. The
rings link at depth where the link stage proves it; each lift has a named
reason. A closed pocket without a safe entry is refused by name.

Under "new", Adaptive, Zigzag (#3753), rest machining (#3753), "do not
touch" areas (#3754) and the corner relief are refused by name. The
switch is still read in one place; run_job_on, generate_on and
GenerateOperation::new_on take the engine for the tests. With the default
switch the old planner runs, unchanged.

The law registry marks the 2D Pocket as moved, with the real stage
planners and the pocket's choices.

Refs #3752

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
